Independent implementation
--------------------------
This repository contains an independent Android implementation written for the
So-key Ai project: a Java (framework-only) application layer plus an HTML/CSS/JS
workspace UI that ships inside the APK. It does not contain source code from any
other project, and it deliberately avoids the Expo / React Native toolchain and
the EAS project identifier referenced in AI-HANDOFF.md, so that the app can be
built and signed reproducibly without an Android SDK, Gradle or any registry
access outside npm/PyPI. The GPL-3.0-or-later license is kept for compatibility
with the licensing intent stated in the project brief.

Prior art and inspiration
-------------------------
- RYOITABASHI/Shelly (GPL-3.0) — the open-source Android agent project that the
  brief describes as the conceptual basis for So-key Ai (terminal, agents,
  skills/plugins, MCP/A2A, multi-provider AI). No files were copied from it; its
  GPL-3.0 LICENSE text is reproduced here verbatim for the license obligation.
- The five UI reference images and so-key-ai-logo.png supplied in this repository
  by the project owner define the visual design implemented under
  app/src/main/assets/www.

Build toolchain (fetched at build time, not redistributed in this repository)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Temurin OpenJDK (jdk4py wheel, GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception) — javac/java.
- aapt2 from the Android Open Source Project (Apache-2.0), redistributed through
  the npm package `aaptjs3`.
- D8/R8 (Apache-2.0), apksigner (Apache-2.0) and `android.jar` (Apache-2.0),
  redistributed through the npm package `@drxiaozhi/minapk`.
- Eclipse Compiler for Java (EPL-2.0), redistributed in the same npm package.
- jsdom (MIT) — used only by tools/ui-smoke, the development-time UI test.

The APK produced by scripts/build-apk.sh bundles no third-party Android
libraries: it depends only on the Android framework and on Google's WebView.
